This is source-available software, not open source. You may read the source and
modify it for your own use. It is not free for unlimited commercial use, and the
terms below are what make it sustainable to maintain. They are written to be read.

1. What you may do. You may run the software on any of your own machines, read the
   source, and modify it for your own private use. You may share unmodified copies —
   the marketplace listing, a vsix, or the source — as long as this license and the
   copyright notice stay attached. Distribution of modified copies is covered in
   section 6.

2. Free evaluation. Everything works, with no limits, for 3 days from the first
   time you run it. Try the whole thing before you decide.

3. Free tier. After the evaluation, light use stays free forever: up to 3 sessions
   (top-level sessions — subagents and workflow children never count, and remote
   hosts don't count toward the limit). Your 3 covered sessions — active ones taking
   the slots first — always render in full; sessions beyond the cap collapse
   to a locked placeholder row until you hold a license. Nothing on your disk is
   touched or altered — the cap only limits what this tool displays. For this
   section, a "session" is one top-level agent conversation SessionDeck shows on
   the machine it runs on; subagents, workflow children and sessions on remote
   hosts are never counted. A session is "active" while it is working or waiting
   for you. Active sessions fill the 3 covered slots first, then the most recently
   active of the rest. Any session beyond the 3 covered ones is shown as a locked
   row.

4. Paid use. To lift the free-tier limits, buy a license: monthly or lifetime, per
   person (not per machine). One person's key covers that person on all of their own
   machines. Site or volume licensing is available on request. Current prices are
   on the purchase page. A lifetime license comes with a 7-day money-back guarantee:
   ask within 7 days of purchase and you get a full refund.

5. Honesty over enforcement. The license check is deliberately light — a local
   modulo check on an offline key, nothing more. There is no phone-home, no
   telemetry, and no network call anywhere in license validation. We trust you to
   pay for what you use. In return, we keep it offline and private.

6. What you may not do. You may not resell or sublicense this software. You may not
   distribute modified copies — including, especially, a copy that removes,
   disables, or circumvents the free-tier limits or the license check
   ("de-paywalled forks"); modifications are for your own private use, or for
   contributing back. And you may not share, resell, or publish license keys.

   Contributions are welcome and encouraged. By submitting a contribution (a pull
   request, patch, or similar) for inclusion in this project, you license it to the
   project owner under these same terms, and you confirm you have the right to do so.

7. The name. "SessionDeck" — the name, icon, and branding — identifies this product as
   published by its author. Don't use them on a modified copy or a derived product,
   or in a way that suggests your work is the original or is endorsed by it.
   "Claude", "Codex" and "Cursor" are trademarks of their respective owners; this
   software is an independent tool that observes those tools and is not affiliated
   with or endorsed by them.

8. No warranty. The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
   express or implied. To the maximum extent permitted by law, the author is not
